@title AWS landing zone network, us-east-2
@subtitle Alderwood Health Analytics cloud team, last reviewed 2026-10-09

## Overview
Three accounts are joined by a transit gateway. All internet-bound traffic is inspected before it leaves. A Direct Connect link runs back to our Columbus data center.

## Network diagram
diagram lz dir=LR title="Landing zone network, us-east-2"
lz: tgw "Transit Gateway" svc focus
lz: fw "Network Firewall" svc focus
lz: nat "NAT Gateway" svc
lz: api "Claims API" svc "ECS"
lz: db "Claims DB" db "Aurora"
lz: stg "Claims API Staging" svc
lz: col "Columbus Data Center" ext
lz: net "Internet" ext
lz: group insp "Inspection VPC 10.0.0.0/16" fw, nat
lz: group netacct "Network account" tgw, insp
lz: group prodvpc "Claims VPC 10.10.0.0/16" api, db
lz: group prod "Prod account" prodvpc
lz: group stgvpc "Staging VPC 10.20.0.0/16" stg
lz: group stgacct "Staging account" stgvpc
lz: prodvpc -> tgw : attachment
lz: stgvpc -> tgw : attachment
lz: tgw -> insp : egress inspection
lz: insp -> net : via NAT
lz: col -> tgw : Direct Connect, 2 x 1 Gbps
lz: api -> db : port 5432

## Address plan
table = VPC,account,CIDR,subnet layout; Inspection VPC,Network,10.0.0.0/16,2 firewall subnets and 2 NAT subnets; Claims VPC,Prod,10.10.0.0/16,3 private app subnets and 3 data subnets; Staging VPC,Staging,10.20.0.0/16,2 private app subnets and 2 data subnets

## Routing rules
!! Staging may never route to prod. This is the rule auditors ask about, so check it first.

- No internet gateways in workload VPCs.
- The Direct Connect link reaches prod only.
